  "description": "Canonical form (RFC 8785), value equality and graph equality. `numbers` and `values` give JSON text and its canonical text, or the error. Any two `equality_samples` are equal exactly when their canonical texts are equal. `graphs` give two graphs, whether they are equal, and each one's graph_hash. `handles` give a handle value and the object it parses to, or null. Each case names the rule it checks in `rule`; README.md lists the rules. The expected outputs are reviewed data that every engine must meet.",
